@event infirmary_missed_round
# en: The Lamp That Went Out
title [6678b7] = 熄灭的灯
# en: The fever charm over the far bed has burned down to a red glow. It should have been turned an hour ago. Sister Amaranth does every round herself, and has never once missed one. Her lamp is dark.
text [980ef1] = 最里面那张床上方的退热符已经烧成一点暗红。一个钟头前就该转了。阿玛兰斯修女每一轮巡房都亲自去，从没漏过一次。她的灯是暗的。
# en: A dim infirmary ward at evening, a fever charm over the far bed glowing a dull red, a healer's desk lamp unlit.
scene [6a0e30] = 黄昏时昏暗的医务室病房，最里面那张床上方的退热符泛着暗红的光，医师桌上的灯没有点。
# en: Turn the charm and find her
opt.left.label [347861] = 转好符，去找她
# en: You turn the charm the way you've seen her do it, a quarter-turn and a tap. Then you go looking for the lamp.
opt.left.say.1 [973261] = 你照她平时的样子转动那道符，转四分之一圈，再轻轻一点。然后你去找那盏灯。
# en: It isn't your ward
opt.right.label [c6562a] = 这不是你的病房
# en: You tell yourself she's only late. On your way out, the patient in the far bed is still awake, watching the dark.
opt.right.say.1 [a9f3b8] = 你告诉自己她只是来晚了。出门时，最里面那张床的病人还醒着，盯着黑暗。

@event infirmary_sister_fevered
# en: The Healer's Own Fever
title [3f2185] = 医师自己的高烧
# en: You find her in the little office behind the ward, upright in her chair, a cold compress on her own neck and the patient list in her lap. Her face is grey. "Lake Fever," she says. "From bed six. It's nothing. Go to bed."
text [14ad94] = 你在病房后面那间小办公室里找到她。她在椅子上坐得笔直，自己脖子上敷着冷毛巾，腿上摊着病人名单。她脸色发灰。“湖热病，”她说，“六号床传的。没什么。去睡觉。”
# en: A small office behind a hospital ward, a grey-faced healer upright in her chair with a compress on her neck and a list of patients in her lap.
scene [3c4215] = 病房后面的一间小办公室，面色发灰的医师在椅子上坐得笔直，脖子上敷着毛巾，腿上放着病人名单。
# en: Fetch the Headmistress
opt.left.label [f62300] = 去叫院长
# en: The headmistress comes in her dressing gown, and two healers from the village by morning. Sister Amaranth doesn't speak to you for a week. Then she thanks you, as an instruction: "Next time, run faster."
opt.left.say.1 [fc5764] = 院长穿着睡袍赶来，天亮前村里又来了两位医师。阿玛兰斯修女整整一周不跟你说话。然后她谢了你，用的是吩咐的口气：“下次跑快点。”
# en: Do the rounds she dictates
opt.right.label [069257] = 照她口述去巡房
# en: "Bed two, the blue bottle, half a spoon. Bed four, turn the charm. Bed six…" She stops. "Bed six will lie to you. Don't believe her." You do the rounds until midnight.
opt.right.say.1 [080508] = “二号床，蓝瓶子，半勺。四号床，转符。六号床……”她顿了一下，“六号床会骗你。别信她。”你一直巡到半夜。

@event infirmary_covering_rounds
# en: Eight Beds, One of You
title [49dfde] = 八张床，一个你
# en: {flag(rounds_secret): Sister Amaranth still can't stand, and is still giving orders from her chair.|The village healers are run off their feet, and Sister Amaranth, propped up in her chair, is giving them orders too.} Eight beds, eight remedies, one of you. A second-year with a burned hand wants to know if it will scar.
text [a5133b] = {flag(rounds_secret): 阿玛兰斯修女还是站不起来，还是坐在椅子上发号施令。|村里来的医师忙得脚不沾地，阿玛兰斯修女靠在椅子上，连他们也一起指挥。} 八张床，八种药，只有你一个人。一个手被烫伤的二年级生想知道会不会留疤。
# en: A row of infirmary beds at evening, a student in rolled-up sleeves measuring a remedy while a healer gives orders from a chair.
scene [856bc9] = 黄昏的一排病床，一个挽着袖子的学生正在量药，一位医师坐在椅子上指挥。
# en: Do every bed properly
opt.left.label [b70095] = 每张床都照顾周全
# en: Every bed, every spoon, every charm turned on the hour. The burned hand won't scar. "Adequate," says the chair, which from her is a medal.
opt.left.say.1 [1330bd] = 每张床、每一勺、每道符都准点转好。烫伤不会留疤。“还行。”椅子上的人说。从她嘴里出来，这就是勋章。
# en: You mix up beds three and five. Nobody notices but her. "Again," she says, and you do the whole row again.
opt.left.say.2 [927a2b] = 你把三号床和五号床弄混了。除了她谁也没发现。“重来。”她说。于是你把整排重做了一遍。
# en: Do the urgent ones, then revise
opt.right.label [7b2a0a] = 先顾急的，再去复习
# en: You see to the burns and the fevers and leave the rest for the morning. From the chair comes a small, disappointed silence.
opt.right.say.1 [469acd] = 你处理好烫伤和高烧，其余的留到早上。椅子那边传来一阵小小的、失望的沉默。

@event lakeshore_fever_runaway
# en: Bed Six Goes Missing
title [5ed052] = 六号床不见了
# en: Bed six is empty, and the window by it is open. You find her where Sister Amaranth said you would: knee-deep in the lake at dusk, shivering, feeling along the bottom. "I lost my mother's ring," the first-year says through chattering teeth. "Swimming. Where we weren't supposed to."
text [7a0322] = 六号床空着，旁边的窗开着。你在阿玛兰斯修女说的地方找到了她：黄昏里，她站在没膝的湖水中，浑身发抖，在湖底摸索。“我把妈妈的戒指弄丢了，”那个一年级生牙齿打着战说，“游泳的时候。在不该游的地方。”
# en: A first-year in a hospital nightshirt standing knee-deep in a dark lake at dusk, feeling along the bottom with both hands.
scene [4aa4c5] = 黄昏时，一个穿病号睡衣的一年级生站在没膝深的黑色湖水里，双手在湖底摸索。
# en: Wade in and search with her
opt.left.label [6566cf] = 下水陪她一起找
# en: Your fingers close on it among the reeds: a thin silver band, slippery with weed. She stops shivering long enough to cry. You both walk back dripping.
opt.left.say.1 [eb5819] = 你的手指在芦苇丛里碰到了它：一枚细细的银戒，裹着滑溜溜的水草。她停止发抖，哭了一会儿。你们俩湿淋淋地走回去。
# en: Nothing but cold and stones. When her lips go blue you carry her back up the hill, and Sister Amaranth's face says everything her fever won't let her.
opt.left.say.2 [c7556f] = 除了冰冷和石头什么也没有。等她嘴唇发紫，你把她背上山。阿玛兰斯修女的脸色说出了高烧不让她说的一切。
# en: Talk her back to bed
opt.right.label [0a087b] = 劝她回去躺着
# en: You promise to look for it in daylight, and she lets you walk her back. Next morning you rake the shallows with a borrowed net, and find the ring on the third pass.
opt.right.say.1 [1fc72f] = 你答应天亮了再来找，她这才让你扶她回去。第二天早上，你借了一张网耙遍浅滩，第三遍时找到了戒指。
# en: She won't come. You wait on the shore with her until she's too cold to argue, then walk her back with your cloak round her.
opt.right.say.2 [aac12b] = 她不肯走。你陪她在岸边等，直到她冷得没力气争辩，才用斗篷裹着她走回去。

@event infirmary_tonic_key
# en: The Key to the Cupboard
title [c634f9] = 药柜的钥匙
# en: Sister Amaranth is back on her feet, doing her evening round as if nothing happened. At the end of it she stops at the tonic cupboard, unhooks a small brass key and holds it out without looking at you. {flag(ring_found): Bed six wears a silver ring on a string round her neck.|Bed six is asleep, for once.}
text [521e2f] = 阿玛兰斯修女又站起来了，照常做她的晚间巡房，仿佛什么都没发生过。巡完后她在药柜前停下，摘下一把小小的黄铜钥匙递过来，看都不看你。{flag(ring_found): 六号床的脖子上用绳子挂着一枚银戒。|六号床难得睡着了。}
# en: A healer on her evening round holding out a small brass key beside a glass-fronted cupboard of tonics, not looking at the student she offers it to.
scene [6e1291] = 晚间巡房的医师站在玻璃门药柜旁，递出一把小黄铜钥匙，没有看向她递给的那个学生。
# en: Take the key
opt.left.label [de2dea] = 接过钥匙
# en: "Keep doing that," she says. It's the most anyone has ever said to you in this room. The key is warm from her pocket.
opt.left.say.1 [a4814c] = “接着这么做。”她说。在这间屋子里，这是任何人对你说过的最多的话。钥匙上还带着她口袋里的温度。
# en: "I'd rather not be trusted with it."
opt.right.label [1b82b9] = “我还是别担这个信任了。”
# en: She hangs it back on its hook. "Good answer," she says. "Wrong, but good." She gives you a tonic anyway, the good one.
opt.right.say.1 [b960d8] = 她把钥匙挂回钩子上。“回答得好，”她说，“错了，但好。”她还是给了你一瓶药，好的那种。

@event lecture_tower_red_ink
# en: Two Sets of Marks
title [8b53b5] = 两种批改
# en: Your returned essay has two sets of marks. The marker's, in polite pencil: "Good." And another, in red ink and unsigned, savaging every paragraph and fixing three of them. The last line reads: "Again. Properly."
text [8582d4] = 发回来的论文上有两种批改。阅卷人用的是客气的铅笔：“好。”另一种是红墨水，没有署名，把每一段都批得体无完肤，还顺手改好了三段。最后一行写着：“重写。认真点。”
# en: A student on a spiral stair reading an essay covered in neat pencil and, beneath it, furious corrections in red ink.
scene [580e72] = 一个学生坐在螺旋楼梯上，读着一篇论文，上面是工整的铅笔批注，底下是怒气冲冲的红墨水修改。
# en: Rewrite it properly
opt.left.label [ddefc9] = 认真重写
# en: You rewrite it twice. On the third morning you leave it on the second-floor stair, where you found the first. By evening it's gone.
opt.left.say.1 [874517] = 你重写了两遍。第三天早上，你把它放在二楼楼梯上，就是你捡到第一份的地方。到傍晚，它不见了。
# en: Bin it
opt.right.label [0a2a07] = 扔掉
# en: Good is good. You drop the red pages in the scorched-room bin, and feel a little foolish about how much you want to fish them out.
opt.right.say.1 [20fc67] = “好”就是好。你把那几页红字丢进烧焦教室的废纸篓，又有点难为情地发现，自己多想把它们捡回来。

@event lecture_tower_red_ink_reply
# en: A Question in the Margin
title [a0e86a] = 页边的问题
# en: The essay is back on the stair, bleeding red. Most of it is about your argument. At the bottom, smaller: "Why do you want to be good at this?" It's the first question the ink has asked.
text [630977] = 论文又回到了楼梯上，满纸红字。大部分是在说你的论证。最底下，字小了些：“你为什么想把这件事做好？”这是红墨水第一次提问。
# en: An essay left on a stone stair, its pages bleeding red ink, a single question written small at the bottom of the last page.
scene [bdf66c] = 一篇论文放在石阶上，纸页上满是红墨水，最后一页底部用小字写着一个问题。
# en: Answer it honestly in the margin
opt.left.label [e7dc4e] = 在页边老实作答
# en: You write three lines you'd never say aloud, and leave the essay on the stair. It's gone by noon. You spend the afternoon wishing you'd written two.
opt.left.say.1 [9ace38] = 你写下三行永远不会说出口的话，把论文留在楼梯上。中午前它就不见了。你一下午都在后悔，应该只写两行。
# en: Wait on the stair to see who takes it
opt.right.label [0b86d8] = 守在楼梯看谁来取
# en: You hide one flight up. A grey sleeve, scorched at the cuff, gathers the pages without a sound. You know exactly one person whose cuffs are scorched.
opt.right.say.1 [0c1944] = 你躲在上一层。一只灰色的袖子，袖口烧焦了，悄无声息地收走了纸页。袖口烧焦的人，你只认识一个。
# en: You fall asleep on the stair. When you wake the essay is gone, and there's a note on your chest: "Hm."
opt.right.say.2 [568b56] = 你在楼梯上睡着了。醒来时论文已经不见，胸口放着一张字条：“嗯。”

@event lecture_tower_red_ink_tremble
# en: The Reading List
title [bc0848] = 书单
# en: This time the red ink answers at length: four pages on your essay, and a reading list. The downstrokes waver, as if written in a moving carriage. {seen(thorne_shaking_hands) > 0: You've seen hands shake like that, gripping a lectern.|On the lower floors, Professor Thorne writes on the board very slowly these days, and very large.}
text [e75d1a] = 这一次红墨水写了很多：四页关于你论文的意见，外加一张书单。竖笔一笔一笔地发颤，像是在颠簸的马车里写的。{seen(thorne_shaking_hands) > 0: 你见过抖成这样的手，紧紧抓着讲台。|在楼下几层，索恩教授如今在黑板上写字写得很慢，也写得很大。}
# en: Four pages of red-ink notes spread on a desk, the downstrokes of the handwriting wavering, a long reading list pinned on top.
scene [7615ba] = 四页红墨水笔记摊在桌上，字迹的竖笔微微发颤，一张长长的书单别在最上面。
# en: Read the whole list
opt.left.label [12a39f] = 把书单读完
# en: You read every book on the list, mostly at night. One has a library card stamped forty years ago, with a single name on it: A. Thorne.
opt.left.say.1 [1bf8cd] = 书单上的每本书你都读了，大多是在夜里。其中一本的借书卡盖着四十年前的章，上面只有一个名字：A. 索恩。
# en: Take the notes, skip the list
opt.right.label [b0da70] = 只看笔记，不看书单
# en: You take the notes and leave the reading list in your satchel. It looks at you every time you open it.
opt.right.say.1 [88b5a3] = 你收下笔记，把书单留在书包里。每次打开书包，它都在看着你。

@event lecture_tower_red_ink_office
# en: Improper Marking
title [5167fa] = 不合规矩的批改
# en: Office hours. You put the stack of red-inked essays on Thorne's desk. He looks at them a long time. "Improper," he says. "Marking essays that aren't mine. I write very few letters, you understand. I like to know who I'm writing them for."
text [53ac38] = 答疑时间。你把那一沓红字论文放在索恩的桌上。他看了很久。“不合规矩，”他说，“批改不归我管的论文。我写的推荐信很少，你明白。我想知道我是在为谁写。”
# en: An old professor at a cluttered office desk looking down at a stack of red-inked essays, a capped red pen in his trembling hand.
scene [7d3878] = 一位老教授坐在杂乱的办公桌前，低头看着一沓红墨水批改过的论文，发颤的手里握着一支盖好笔帽的红笔。
# en: "Then write one for me."
opt.left.label [250c84] = “那就为我写一封。”
# en: "Hm." From him, that's a yes. The letter, when it goes, is four lines long. The Conclave, you hear later, read it twice.
opt.left.say.1 [069460] = “嗯。”从他嘴里出来，这就是答应了。那封信寄出时只有四行。后来你听说，七塔议会把它读了两遍。
# en: "Not yet," he says. "Again. Properly." It takes you a day to understand that it was a promise.
opt.left.say.2 [7b33c7] = “还不行，”他说，“重写。认真点。”你过了一天才明白，那是一个承诺。
# en: "Thank you. Keep marking them."
opt.right.label [2fd45e] = “谢谢您。请继续批。”
# en: He nods once. The red ink keeps coming to the end of the year. It never once says "good". Once, it says "better".
opt.right.say.1 [26c4c3] = 他点了一下头。红墨水一直来到学年结束。它一次也没写过“好”。有一次，它写了“好些了”。

@event home_market_late_bloomer
# en: Blue Candles
title [8f5833] = 蓝色的蜡烛
# en: The sweet shop is the one thing in town that hasn't changed. Then the owner's daughter, a year or two older than you, drops a tray, swears, and every candle in the window flares blue. Her father looks at you, then at your castle robes. "You're the one who'd know," he says quietly.
text [0b982b] = 糖果铺是镇上唯一没变的地方。接着，店主的女儿——比你大一两岁——打翻了托盘，骂了一句，橱窗里所有的蜡烛都蹿起了蓝火。她父亲看看你，又看看你身上的城堡学袍。“你是懂这个的人。”他低声说。
# en: A small sweet shop window full of jars, every candle in it flaring blue, a young woman staring at her own hands beside a dropped tray.
scene [be34a6] = 一家摆满糖罐的小糖果铺橱窗，里面每支蜡烛都蹿着蓝火，一个年轻女人站在打翻的托盘旁，盯着自己的双手。
# en: Show her how to breathe it down
opt.left.label [1a87b0] = 教她把它压下去
# en: You show her the first thing anyone at the castle learns: breathe in for four, hold the heat, let it go for four. The candles settle. She looks at her hands as if they belonged to someone else.
opt.left.say.1 [775fd7] = 你教她城堡里每个人学的第一件事：吸气数四下，把热憋住，呼气再数四下。蜡烛安静下来了。她看着自己的手，像是在看别人的手。
# en: "It happens. It'll settle."
opt.right.label [6cc646] = “常有的事。会过去的。”
# en: Her father nods, glad to be told so. Behind him she relights the candles one by one, with a match, very carefully.
opt.right.say.1 [7c1f9e] = 她父亲点点头，很高兴听到这话。在他身后，她用火柴把蜡烛一支一支重新点上，非常小心。

@event home_fields_bloomer_lessons
# en: Lessons on the Wall
title [844754] = 墙头上的课
# en: She's waiting on the low wall at the end of the long rows, a candle stub in each pocket. "Teach me something," she says. "Properly. Before you go back."
text [e60081] = 她在长长田垄尽头的矮墙上等着，两个口袋里各揣着一截蜡烛头。“教我点东西，”她说，“认真地教。趁你还没回去。”
# en: A young woman and a student in castle robes on a low field wall at sunset, the young woman holding a candle stub at arm's length, its flame far too tall.
scene [22636a] = 日落时，一个年轻女人和一个穿城堡学袍的学生坐在田边矮墙上，年轻女人伸直手臂举着一截蜡烛头，火苗高得过分。
# en: Teach her the candle drill
opt.left.label [b8469a] = 教她蜡烛练习
# en: By sunset she can hold a flame the size of a fingernail for ten breaths. She counts every one of them out loud.
opt.left.say.1 [19772d] = 到日落时，她已经能让指甲盖大小的火苗稳住十次呼吸。她每一下都大声数出来。
# en: The candle goes off like a firework. You both lie in the grass laughing until the farmer shouts. "Next time," she says.
opt.left.say.2 [de9e7a] = 蜡烛像烟花一样炸开了。你们俩躺在草地上笑，直到农夫开骂。“下次吧。”她说。
# en: Spend the afternoon at home
opt.right.label [177620] = 下午留在家里
# en: You promise her next time. She shrugs, the way people do when they've stopped expecting things.
opt.right.say.1 [f41615] = 你答应她下次。她耸耸肩，就像人们已经不再指望什么时那样。

@event home_cottage_bloomer_father
# en: Sweets on the Step
title [a4badc] = 台阶上的糖
# en: Her father is at the door with a paper bag of the sweets you liked when you were small. He doesn't come in. "They take them young, at the castle, don't they," he says. "She's past it. So what is it for, all that fire, in a sweet shop?"
text [1d4d9f] = 她父亲站在门口，拿着一小纸袋你小时候爱吃的糖。他没有进来。“城堡收的都是年纪小的，是吧，”他说，“她已经过了那个年纪。那一身的火，在糖果铺里有什么用？”
# en: A worried shopkeeper at a cottage door holding a small paper bag of sweets, not stepping inside.
scene [9f38ed] = 一个忧心忡忡的店主站在小屋门口，拿着一小纸袋糖，没有进门。
# en: Tell him the truth
opt.left.label [48bf7e] = 对他说实话
# en: "I don't know what it's for," you tell him. "I don't think anyone does, at her age." He thanks you for not lying, and leaves the sweets on the step.
opt.left.say.1 [98beb1] = “我不知道有什么用，”你告诉他，“到了她这个年纪，我想谁也不知道。”他谢谢你没有骗他，把糖留在了台阶上。
# en: Promise to ask at the castle
opt.right.label [aafec0] = 答应去城堡问问
# en: His face does something complicated. "Would you," he says, not quite a question. You hear yourself promise. The sweets taste exactly as they used to.
opt.right.say.1 [e74743] = 他的脸上掠过很复杂的神情。“你会吗。”他说，不太像是在问。你听见自己答应了。那些糖的味道和从前一模一样。

@event home_market_bloomer_charm
# en: A Lid on the Pot
title [f09a76] = 锅上的盖子
# en: In the market you find her at the charm seller's table. He's holding up a grey glass bead on a cord. "Smothers it," he's saying. "Like a lid on a pot. No more flares, no more fuss." She's counting out her savings.
text [3ffde8] = 你在集市上卖护身符的人的摊子前找到了她。他举着一颗系在绳上的灰色玻璃珠。“能把它闷住，”他说，“就像给锅盖上盖子。不再冒火，不再添乱。”她正在数自己攒下的钱。
# en: A market charm seller holding up a grey glass bead on a cord to a young woman counting coins from her apron.
scene [97e8d2] = 集市上卖护身符的人举着一颗系着绳的灰色玻璃珠，一个年轻女人正从围裙里数出硬币。
# en: Help her pay, since she wants it
opt.left.label [0f543f] = 她想要，就帮她付
# en: You make up what she's short, because it's her choice. She puts the bead on. The shop's candles burn an ordinary yellow from then on. She looks lighter, and smaller.
opt.left.say.1 [74e4f3] = 你补上她差的钱，因为这是她的选择。她戴上了珠子。从那以后，店里的蜡烛只烧出普通的黄色火苗。她看起来轻松了，也变小了。
# en: Talk her out of it
opt.right.label [7db2be] = 劝她别买
# en: You tell her about the first-years who set their sleeves alight and are now the best in their year. She puts her coins back in her apron, slowly.
opt.right.say.1 [be605f] = 你给她讲那些把袖子点着了的一年级生，如今都是年级里最出色的。她慢慢把硬币放回了围裙。
# en: She buys it anyway. "Easy for you," she says, not unkindly. "You get to go back."
opt.right.say.2 [d6500c] = 她还是买了。“你说得轻巧，”她说，并没有恶意，“你还能回去。”

@event home_market_bloomer_ice
# en: Ice in the Square
title [44b78b] = 广场上的冰
# en: Not ten minutes later, a shout from the square. The horse trough has frozen solid, with a carter's arm in it to the elbow, and she's standing beside it white with panic. Frost is creeping across the cobbles from her feet.
text [6aaab7] = 不到十分钟，广场上传来一声大喊。饮马槽冻得结结实实，一个车夫的胳膊冻在里面，一直冻到手肘。她站在旁边，吓得脸色发白。霜正从她脚下爬过石板路。
# en: A market-square horse trough frozen solid around a carter's arm, a panicking young woman beside it and frost spreading across the cobbles.
scene [4e5996] = 集市广场上的饮马槽冻得结结实实，把一个车夫的胳膊封在里面，一个惊慌的年轻女人站在一旁，霜在石板路上蔓延。
# en: Break the ice by hand
opt.left.label [fe2922] = 用手砸开冰
# en: You hammer at the ice with a cobble until it gives with a crack like a door. The carter pulls his arm free, swearing, mostly at the trough.
opt.left.say.1 [280b1c] = 你抄起一块铺路石砸冰，直到它像一扇门一样咔嚓一声裂开。车夫抽出胳膊，骂骂咧咧，主要是在骂那个饮马槽。
# en: You get him free in the end, but the ice takes the skin off your knuckles doing it. You'll feel that trough for days.
opt.left.say.2 [f780c2] = 你最后还是把他弄了出来，可冰把你的指节磨掉了一层皮。那个饮马槽你得疼上好几天。
# en: Talk her down so it melts
opt.right.label [2bd1f0] = 安抚她让冰化开
# en: "Four in. Hold. Four out." Her breath slows, and the ice goes grey, then soft, then water. The carter stares at his arm, and then at her.
opt.right.say.1 [62e526] = “吸气四下。憋住。呼气四下。”她的呼吸慢下来，冰变灰，变软，化成了水。车夫盯着自己的胳膊，又盯着她。
# en: It takes an hour, three kettles from the inn and a carter who will tell this story for years.
opt.right.say.2 [25f257] = 花了一个钟头、旅店的三壶热水，还造就了一个会把这事讲上好多年的车夫。

@event home_cottage_bloomer_letter
# en: A Flame That Stays
title [62c792] = 不灭的火苗
# en: {flag(bloomer_damped): She comes by one evening, the grey bead on its cord. "I keep it in my pocket now," she says. "Not on. Just in case." She lights a candle with her finger, small and steady, to show you.|She comes by one evening with a candle she lit at noon and has kept burning, small and steady, all day. "Look," she says. "It stays."}
text [a4fdcf] = {flag(bloomer_damped): 一天傍晚她来了，那颗灰珠子用绳子系着。“我现在把它放在口袋里，”她说，“不戴。只是以防万一。”她用手指点亮一支蜡烛给你看，火苗小而稳。|一天傍晚她来了，带着一支中午点燃、一直烧到现在的蜡烛，火苗小而稳。“你看，”她说，“它不灭了。”}
# en: A young woman at a cottage table at evening, a small steady candle flame burning on the tip of her finger.
scene [a44cc7] = 傍晚，一个年轻女人坐在小屋的桌旁，指尖上燃着一朵小小的、稳定的烛火。
# en: Write to the castle for her
opt.left.label [3d556e] = 替她给城堡写信
# en: {flag(bloomer_promise): You keep your promise to her father and write to the castle that night|You write to the castle that night}: what she can do, what she learned with no teacher but you, and that some people come late to things. You pay the postage; she walks it to the post office herself.
opt.left.say.1 [e70f80] = {flag(bloomer_promise): 你遵守了对她父亲的承诺，当晚就给城堡写了信|当晚你给城堡写了信}：她能做什么，她在除了你之外没有老师的情况下学会了什么，还有，有些人就是来得晚一些。邮费你付了；信是她自己走去邮局寄的。
# en: Give her your first-year book
opt.right.label [d6667b] = 把一年级课本给她
# en: {flag(bloomer_promise): You never did ask at the castle. Instead you leave her your battered first-year book, margins and all.|You leave her your battered first-year book, margins and all.} A week later a letter comes: "Your notes are wrong. I've fixed them."
opt.right.say.1 [5e94e2] = {flag(bloomer_promise): 你终究没有去城堡问。你把那本破旧的一年级课本留给了她，连同页边的笔记。|你把那本破旧的一年级课本留给了她，连同页边的笔记。}一周后来了一封信：“你的笔记写错了。我改好了。”
